class.description:
Moves a character (its [JRPGMover], with its [JRPGEventState], where the route position and pause are saved) by itself, as its event page says ([method set_page_movement]):
- fixed: it stays put;
- random: a step in a random direction;
- approach: a step along the shortest way to a cell next to the player (searched through at most [constant PATH_SEARCH_LIMIT] cells); without one, along the longer axis toward the player, then the other, then a random step;
- custom: the page's [JRPGMoveRoute], one step at a time.
After each move it pauses as its frequency says: 240, 120, 60, 30 or 0 steps for frequencies 1 to 5, plus 0 to [constant RANDOM_PAUSE_MAX] steps drawn from the game's map AI stream so crowds do not move in step. A route [method force_route] gives runs instead, without pauses, until it ends.
Route commands that take no time (turns, switches, speed...) run together, up to [constant MAX_INSTANT_COMMANDS] a step. A blocked move waits for the way to clear unless the route is skippable. Direction fix keeps the facing through moves and turns. The caller advances the mover each step before [method update_step]; a character still moving does nothing new. Everything is drawn from the given random stream, so the same game moves the same way on every machine.
Authority: server.
